course: dictionary
lesson: 15397
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The clues in the sentence show you which meaning the writer wants. «It's only spitting, so bring an umbrella but not your swimming costume.» Spitting means raining very lightly, because only and umbrella show that the rain is small.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in another sentence. «The sausages were spitting in the hot pan.» Spitting does not mean spit coming out of a mouth here. The fat is making tiny hot bursts, so the word means that. Always ask: what is happening in this sentence?
explain: Some words belong to set phrases, like «spitting image» and «spitting distance». The phrase has its own meaning, so you cannot work it out word by word. «Ella is the spitting image of her mum» means Ella looks exactly like her mum.
fact: Spitting is the -ing form of spit, and it can be a verb, a noun or an adjective.
fact: Spitting can mean forcing spit or food out of your mouth, and spitting at people is rude and unhygienic.
fact: In the UK and Ireland, «it's spitting» means it is raining very lightly, with just a few drops.
fact: Spitting can also mean making small hot bursts or sparks, like fat in a pan or a fire.
fact: «Spitting image» means looking exactly like someone, and «spitting distance» means very close.
exercise: «It's only spitting, so you won't need your big coat.» What does spitting mean here? | *Raining very lightly | Forcing spit out of your mouth | Making tiny sparks in a fire | Hissing angrily like a cat
exercise: «The sausages were spitting in the hot pan.» What is spitting doing here? | Raining very lightly | *Making small hot bursts of fat | Looking exactly like someone | Hissing angrily
exercise: «The cat was spitting at the dog and arched its back.» What does spitting show about the cat? | Raining very lightly | Sleeping peacefully | *Hissing angrily | Playing with a ball
test: «She is the spitting image of her dad.» What does spitting image mean? | *Looking exactly like someone | Very close to someone | Raining lightly | Spitting out food
test: «The shop was within spitting distance of the station.» What does spitting distance mean? | Raining very lightly | Spitting out food | Very far away | *Very close
exam: Why should you never spit at people? | Because it helps you grow taller | Because it means you are happy | *Because it is rude and unhygienic | Because it makes the rain stop
